# Synthetic ballot reconstruction of the real 2019 Nauruan parliamentary election, Boe
# constituency (5 candidates, 2 seats, 811 voters, Dowdall/Nauru scoring) -- a second,
# independent constituency from the same election as nauru-2019-anabar.blt, used as a
# cross-check that fixture wasn't a fluke. Real per-voter ballots are not published; what IS
# published (Wikipedia's "2019 Nauruan parliamentary election" article, sourced to the
# Electoral Commission of Nauru) is each candidate's vote count at each of the 5 preference
# ranks and their final Dowdall score:
#   Martin Hunt:      261/164/161/130/95  -> 448.167 (elected)
#   Asterio Appi:     204/201/142/174/90  -> 413.333 (re-elected)
#   Baron Waqa:       188/79/58/132/354   -> 350.633
#   Mathew Batsiua:   144/98/189/232/148  -> 343.600
#   Brett Satto:      14/269/261/143/124  -> 296.050
# As with the Anabar fixture, this is a synthetic-but-mathematically-faithful reconstruction:
# Dowdall/Borda scoring is linear in each candidate's own (rank, count) marginal alone, so any
# ballot set reproducing this same marginal table produces IDENTICAL scores to the real
# election. The ballots below (a greedy bipartite-matching decomposition of the table above)
# were verified independently, in Python, before this file was generated, to reproduce all five
# official scores above exactly. See BordaNauru2019BoeFixtureTest.
